# Help: The audit subsystem, for a userspace that starts auditd
# core/systemd.config sets AUDIT=n, as systemd's README advises for a
# system that runs containers. A distribution whose userspace starts
# auditd at boot, as Fedora's does, then has two failed units and a
# boot that ends degraded. Merge this fragment after core/systemd.config
# to build the subsystem with its system call auditing.
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/audit/index.html
CONFIG_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_AUDITSYSCALL=y
